UID:PyZPY71g7sq-rOUHgUI1s
SUMMARY:The future of engineering from Anthropic’s Eng Service Co CTO
DTSTAMP:20260810T100229Z
DTSTART:20260813T190000Z
DESCRIPTION:Register here: https://luma.com/8q74pmn4 \nAI has changed what 
	it means to be an engineer. \nAs GenAI models become capable of tackling i
	ncreasingly complex work\, the value that engineers bring is changing: dec
	iding what should be built\, designing reliable systems\, validating AI-ge
	nerated work\, understanding customers\, and orchestrating agents. The cha
	nges are accelerating. What does this mean for engineers in the future\, a
	nd how does one stay relevant? \nJoin Eddie Siegel\, Co-Founder & CTO of O
	de\, Anthropic’s engineering services company\, for a candid\, unscripted 
	conversation about where engineering is heading\, what skills will matter 
	over the next decade\, and how to cultivate and deploy them. \nBefore Anth
	ropic\, Eddie built engineering organizations at LiveRamp\, Wove\, Samba T
	V\, Xip\, and Fractional AI. Through Fractional AI\, he worked inside doze
	ns of engineering teams deploying production AI systems\, giving him a fro
	nt-row seat to what actually changes when AI moves from ad hoc assistance 
	to firm-wide transformation. \nToday\, Ode is building for that future\, e
	xecuting gargantuan transformative projects yielding millions of dollars f
	or fortune 100 companies. \nTopics we’ll explore:\n– Where AI is heading\,
	 from Anthropic model capabilities to organizational transformation\n– Whe
	re engineering is heading\, and what it means to stay competitive\n– What 
	Ode is doing\, why it’s growing so quickly\, and a look behind the scenes\
	n– Who Ode is hiring and what the firm is looking for to execute under Ant
	hropic\n– Your questions \nWho Should Attend:\nThis event is for software 
	engineers\, engineering leaders\, founders\, computer and data scientists\
	, and anyone thinking seriously about their place in an AI-native future. 
	\nWhether you’re trying to future-proof your career\, understand where eng
	ineering is heading\, or explore opportunities to build the next generatio
	n of developer tools\, this conversation is for you. \nExpect an open conv
	ersation about where engineering is going and the people who will shape wh
	at’s next.\n\nhttps://iondistrict.com/event/the-future-of-engineering-from
	-anthropics-eng-service-co-cto/\n\nFrom Ion District
URL:https://iondistrict.com/event/the-future-of-engineering-from-anthropics
	-eng-service-co-cto/
LOCATION:Zoom
X-CALRIPPER-SOURCE:ion-district
CATEGORIES:Ion District
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
DURATION:PT1H
END:VEVENT
